    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0981" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg861"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">493.11 Shelton, Dr. A. L.: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-03-11T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 11,
                                1922—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 14—10:07
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>96. Legation’s 85, March 7, noon.<anchor n="28" xml:id="d664-f1"/> On 10th I
                    again addressed Foreign Office stating receipt of confirmation of murder which
                    now appeared indubitable. I renewed request use every effort apprehend and try
                    guilty parties speediest possible manner, also requested in view of deep concern
                    American Government I receive earliest possible statement of steps taken by
                    Chinese Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Schurman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
